eration.sign_manifest retry loop (generation.py:317-403)","norm_id":"n32c131225a06f129","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A sign_manifest attempt hits an under-lock mismatch or transient store-read-failure and retries; the second attempt's pre-lock forced fetch is the call's second fetch.","A tester (or reviewer) reads 'exactly once' as a per-call invariant and treats a retried call that fetched twice as a regression."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword AC-3 to 'Each sign_manifest attempt performs at most one fetch, always pre-lock and never while the lock is held; across retries the per-attempt invariant holds' and have the counting test assert one fetch per attempt rather than one per call.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Classify the other gate-material baseline seams — orchestrator.py:480 (feeds attest.refresh_attestation), attest.py:152/288, resign.py:105 — as in-scope (force_fresh=True) or explicitly out-of-scope, rather than leaving them silently throttled.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Pass force_fresh=True at exactly two places: the review-start snapshot in plan_review/__init__.py and the PRE-lock collect in generation.sign_manifest.'","orchestrator.py:480 `initial_generation = generation.collect(ctx.ticket_id, repo_root=repo_root, ignore_untracked=True)` whose result feeds attest.refresh_attestation(..., initial_generation=initial_generation) at orchestrator.py:537 — a throttled read that produces a signing baseline (drift-refresh/reuse path).","attest.py:152 and attest.py:288 call collect_plan_relation_snapshot as a fallback when initial_generation is None.","resign.py:105 `baseline = generation.collect(ticket_id, ...)` for re-sign.","Plan 'Out of scope' enumerates only 'the claim-time currency check, --status, and every non-gate read' — it does not state whether these review/sign-adjacent collect seams are intentionally excluded."],"finding":"The plan forces a fresh fetch at 'exactly two places' (review-start snapshot in plan_review/__init__.py and the pre-lock collect in generation.sign_manifest) but does not enumerate or classify three other gate-material read seams that produce signing/review baselines from the same lagging clone: orchestrator.py:480 (generation.collect → initial_generation → attest.refresh_attestation at 537), attest.py:152/288 (fallback collect_plan_relation_snapshot), and resign.py:105 (generation.collect re-sign baseline). These remain on the 60s throttle and can pin a superseded description — the same defect the plan fixes — yet 'Out of scope' names only the claim-time check, --status, and 'every non-gate read', leaving these unclassified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f51f772c72325de83","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 ('Pass force_fresh=True at exactly two places') and 'Out of scope' paragraph","norm_id":"n395b5a60a23c4696","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The drift-refresh reuse path (orchestrator) re-binds an attestation from a description that is already superseded on origin because the shared throttle marker is fresh.","A re-sign (resign.py) or an attest fallback computes its baseline from the lagging clone within the 60s window."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to 'Out of scope' naming the drift-refresh reuse collect (orchestrator), the attest fallback collect, and the resign baseline collect, and state why they keep the throttle (e.g., they re-bind an already-attested basis, not a fresh review) — or extend step 3 to force them too if they can produce a first signing baseline.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the disposition when the forced pre-lock fetch itself fails (e.g. is it acceptable to sign on the stale clone, or should the fetch failure surface as transient/retryable so the sign is not completed on possibly-stale material), since the `fresh != initial_generation` net cannot catch a fetch that never reached origin.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.57,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'It still honors the opt-outs ... and stays best-effort (a fetch failure is swallowed).'","Plan: 'A drift the pre-lock fetch reveals surfaces through the existing `fresh != initial_generation` check' — this only fires when the fetch SUCCEEDS and reveals drift; a failed forced fetch reveals nothing.","ABSENCE: no disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal) for the case where the forced fetch itself fails and the clone stays stale."],"finding":"The forced pre-lock fetch is best-effort and swallows failures, but the plan's only drift-safety net is the `fresh != initial_generation` check. If the forced fetch FAILS, both the review-start snapshot and the pre-lock re-collect read the same stale clone, so fresh==initial and no PlanReviewGenerationChanged fires — a superseded description is signed silently. The plan does not state the disposition of the swallowed-fetch arm (what the caller surfaces when the force fetch cannot reach origin).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f422136be52ec83cd","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 ('stays best-effort (a fetch failure is swallowed)') and step 4 (PlanReviewGenerationChanged safety net)","norm_id":"n5f4b54eadffb15cb","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Origin has a superseded description; the MCP server's forced pre-lock fetch fails (network/origin unreachable); the clone stays at old HEAD; review-start and under-lock both pin the stale description; generation check passes; stale description is signed with no warning."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{